## 2. Task Tables

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| **AT1** – *Navigate to kitchen* | Robot moves from its current location to the kitchen. | AND (under G2) | kitchen | 1 | Robot must physically reach the kitchen to pick up the meal. |
| **AT2** – *Pick up meal from kitchen* | Robot grasps the requested meal(s). | AND (under G2) | kitchen | 1 | Physical manipulation of the meal is required. |
| **AT3** – *Query patient record* | Robot queries the hospital database for patient’s retrieval capability. | AND (under G3) | hospital database | 1 | Determines if the patient can retrieve the tray. |
| **AT4** – *Check presence of companion or nurse* | Robot checks the room for a companion or nurse who can assist. | AND (under G3) | patient room | 1 | Needed to decide if tray hand‑over is feasible. |
| **AT5** – *Decide delivery method* | Robot decides between table delivery and tray hand‑over. | AND (under G3) | internal | 1 | Uses results of AT3 and AT4. |
| **AT6** – *Navigate to patient room* | Robot moves to the patient’s room. | AND (under G4.1 & G4.2) | patient room | 1 | Required before any delivery action. |
| **AT7** – *Deliver meal to room table* | Robot places the meal on the patient’s table. | AND (under G4.1) | patient room | 1 | Physical placement on the table. |
| **AT8** – *Hand over tray to patient* | Robot hands the meal tray to the patient. | AND (under G4.2) | patient room | 1 | Physical hand‑over. |
| **AT9** – *Assist patient in retrieving tray* | Robot assists the patient in pulling the tray. | AND (under G4.2) | patient room | 1 | Needed if patient cannot retrieve alone. |
| **AT10** – *Indicate meal to patient* | Robot informs the patient which meal is on the tray. | AND (under G4.2) | patient room | 1 | Prevents wrong meal retrieval. |
| **AT11** – *Track meal retrieval* | Robot records when and where the meal is taken. | AND (under G4.2) | patient room | 1 | Enables monitoring of meal delivery. |
| **AT12** – *Alert wrong meal* | Robot alerts the patient if a wrong meal is taken. | AND (under G4.2) | patient room | 1 | Ensures correct meal delivery. |
| **AT13** – *Retrieve dirty dishes (unassisted)* | Robot collects dirty dishes by itself. | AND (under G5.1) | patient room | 1 | Robot can handle dishes alone. |
| **AT14** – *Retrieve dishes with another robot* | Two robots cooperate to collect dishes. | AND (under G5.2) | patient room | 2 | Two robots needed to lift heavy loads. |
| **AT15** – *Retrieve dishes with human* | Robot cooperates with a human to collect dishes. | AND (under G5.3) | patient room | 1 | Human assists with lifting. |
| **AT16** – *Open door alone* | Robot opens the door by itself. | AND (under G6.1) | patient room door | 1 | Robot has door‑opening capability. |
| **AT17** – *Open door with human* | Robot cooperates with a human to open the door. | AND (under G6.2) | patient room door | 1 | Human may need to open latch. |
| **AT18** – *Open door with another robot* | Two robots cooperate to open the door. | AND (under G6.3) | patient room door | 2 | Door may be heavy or locked. |
| **AT19** – *Receive call for dish pickup* | Robot listens for a call from someone in the room. | AND (under G7) | patient room | 1 | Robot must detect the call. |
| **AT20** – *Check if door can be opened* | Robot verifies that the door is unlocked and can be opened. | AND (under G7) | patient room door | 1 | Safety check before opening. |
| **AT21** – *Signal door opening* | Robot signals to the person that the door is open. | AND (under G7) | patient room | 1 | Provides feedback to the caller. |

